## Summary
The TTMIK team is conducting in-person user research interviews to gather feedback on their language learning website. Participants will engage in a 45-minute interview near Hongik University Station, with a reward of 30,000 KRW, and recordings will be used solely for research purposes.

## Key Points
- The TTMIK team is seeking user feedback through in-person interviews for their website.
- Participants receive a 30,000 KRW cash reward immediately after the interview.
- Interviews are conducted in English or Korean near Hongik University Station in Seoul.
- Audio and screen recordings are made for research use only and not shared publicly.
- Selection for interviews is done via a survey form, with notifications sent by email.


